					<description><![CDATA[<p>Enterprise software implementation has hit a massive bottleneck. Companies buy advanced artificial intelligence tools, but integrating them into legacy systems remains slow, costly, and painful. June AI raises $20 million</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/june-ai-raises-20-million-in-pre-seed-funding-to-automate-enterprise-ai-deployment/" data-wpel-link="internal">June AI Raises $20 Million in Pre-Seed Funding To Automate Enterprise AI Deployment</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Enterprise software implementation has hit a massive bottleneck. Companies buy advanced artificial intelligence tools, but integrating them into legacy systems remains slow, costly, and painful. June AI raises $20 million in pre-seed funding to solve this exact problem. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The round was led by Marc Benioff’s TIME Ventures, with participation from prominent technology leaders including Michael Dell, Diane Greene, Aaron Levie, and George Kurtz. The main aim of June AI is to use AI agents to automate complex software deployment across large organizations.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Solving the Enterprise AI Deployment Bottleneck</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The deployment of enterprise software is challenging and labor-intensive. Hundreds of billions of dollars have been invested by global organizations every year to configure, integrate and maintain their core systems. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Businesses are trying to incorporate GPT-style models, but there are years of technical debt that make it difficult to operate. There are very few seamless connections between legacy platforms,  such as SAP, Oracle, Workday, and Salesforce, and modern cloud data infrastructure.</span></p>
<div id="attachment_203957" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203957" class="size-large wp-image-203957" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/June-AI-model-1024x576.jpeg" alt="June AI introduces its unified multi-model platform designed to bring every AI model into one central hub." width="1024" height="576" /><p id="caption-attachment-203957" class="wp-caption-text">Multi-Model AI, Unified. Credit: June AI</p></div>
<p><a href="https://askjune.ai/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">June AI</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> tackles this implementation gap directly. Instead of forcing companies to hire expensive teams of outside consultants, the startup uses AI agents to streamline integration. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform acts as an automated digital bridge. It analyzes how an enterprise operates and automates repetitive configuration tasks, drastically reducing setup timelines for enterprise software.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/base-power-1b-series-d-base-core-battery/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Base Power Raises $1B To Mass Produce Batteries for Homes</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">How June AI Automates Systems Integration</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">June AI begins its process with deep system analysis and process mining. The platform examines existing database logs to uncover how business workflows actually execute inside the organization. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Once it maps these hidden patterns, it identifies operational bottlenecks and automates structural software changes. The technology works natively across major data environments like Databricks and Snowflake. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">By mapping cross-system relationships, June AI ensures that system updates in one department do not break downstream processes. The platform empowers forward-deployed engineers and system integration teams to deploy enterprise AI agents with far less friction and lower overall costs.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The global system integration market is expected to reach over one trillion dollars in the coming decade. As companies increase their AI investments, automated integration will become essential enterprise infrastructure. Advanced foundational AI models offer little value if businesses cannot connect them to their live operational data.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/olix-raises-312m-3-3b-valuation-nvidia-rival/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Olix Raises $312M To Scale Specialized AI Inference Silicon</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Founded by Experienced Salesforce Veterans</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203958" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203958" class="size-large wp-image-203958" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/June-AI-founders-1024x660.jpg" alt="Four members of the June AI team smiling and leaning against a dark metal balcony railing, all wearing matching black June shirts." width="1024" height="660" /><p id="caption-attachment-203958" class="wp-caption-text">June AI Founders: Credit: Omer Hacohen</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The founding team brings deep enterprise software experience to this challenge. June AI is the brainchild of CEO Efrat Rapoport, CTO Idan Tsitiat, President Barak Goldstein, and Chief Architect Ohad Hen. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The founding group earlier developed Bonobo AI, a conversational intelligence platform that was bought by Salesforce back then in 2019. The founders have experienced enterprise friction firsthand as they led key product teams and engineering teams within Salesforce for the past five years.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">They observed that purchasing AI software is relatively easy, but implementing it across fragmented custom workflows is extremely hard. June AI was created to replace manual professional services with automated software workflows, enabling faster time-to-value for modern enterprise buyers.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">With $20 million in new capital and backing from top industry leaders, June AI is well-positioned to pioneer automated deployment. By removing technical debt and speeding up integrations, the company helps enterprises move past simple AI demos into fully functional automated operations.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/revoy-raises-27-million-electric-truck-dolly/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Revoy Raises $27M to Turn Old Diesel Trucks Into Hybrids</i></b></a></p>
