					<description><![CDATA[<p>Horizon3 Raises $250 Million To Advance AI-Driven Cybersecurity Horizon3, an AI-powered cybersecurity firm based in San Francisco, raised $250 million in Series E funding, which it said would be used</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/horizon3-raises-250-million/" data-wpel-link="internal">Horizon3 Raises $250 Million to Expand AI-Powered Cybersecurity Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Horizon3 Raises $250 Million To Advance AI-Driven Cybersecurity</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Horizon3, an AI-powered cybersecurity firm based in San Francisco, raised $250 million in Series E funding, which it said would be used to further its international platform growth around the world. Following the close of the round, the company reached a valuation of more than $2 billion.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its valuation more than tripled compared with approximately $600 million achieved during the previous funding round year. The investment supports expansion of Horizon3&#8217;s AI-native cybersecurity platform across international enterprise markets and customer operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">NightDragon and NEA led the oversubscribed financing alongside existing and new global strategic investors participating together successfully. The company plans accelerating innovation while strengthening proactive cybersecurity capabilities for enterprises facing increasingly </span><a href="https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/sophisticated" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">sophisticated</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> artificial intelligence threats.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Global Expansion And Product Innovation</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding supports global sales, marketing expansion, market growth, and autonomous cybersecurity technology development initiatives worldwide. Horizon3 plans expanding its European presence while entering Singapore and Australia through strategic international market expansion.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company will increase research investment enhancing its NodeZero platform and autonomous artificial intelligence security agents. These autonomous agents automatically identify and remediate cybersecurity vulnerabilities across enterprise information technology environments efficiently today.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Horizon3 will use the investment to strengthen its artificial intelligence-powered proactive security platform and accelerate innovation. The funding follows rising enterprise demand for protection against artificial intelligence-powered cyber threats and evolving compliance requirements.</span></p>
<h2><b>NodeZero Uses AI To Test Enterprise Defences<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203953" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203953" class="size-full wp-image-203953" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-futuristic-poster-depicts-a-swirling-v_E8BUjXA9Xu-LxyDZXLh-Dg_PAteiiPAT4iZf10iaT0vxA.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI-driven cybersecurity systems testing and defending enterprise networks in real time." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203953" class="wp-caption-text">Horizon3 enables continuous AI-powered penetration testing and real-time enterprise threat detection. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Former JSOC colleagues Snehal Antani and Anthony Pillitiere founded Horizon3 to automate penetration testing through NodeZero. NodeZero continuously attacks customer networks using self-driving penetration testing technology to identify cybersecurity vulnerabilities proactively everywhere.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Unlike annual assessments, the platform safely tests live production environments using fully automated security testing capabilities continuously. It helps enterprises discover attack paths, prioritise security weaknesses, and implement effective remediation measures quickly and efficiently.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company said it has completed more than 310,000 production security tests across enterprise customer environments globally. Unlike traditional testers, Horizon3 evaluates complete enterprise infrastructures while production systems continue operating without interruption successfully.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its platform also includes intelligent honeypots helping organisations detect active attackers targeting enterprise systems in real time. More than 7,000 enterprises currently use the platform across banking, healthcare, government, and Fortune 10 organisations worldwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/dash-bio-raises-30-million/" data-wpel-link="internal">Dash Bio Raises $30 Million to Modernise Drug Development Infrastructure</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Enterprise Demand Accelerates As AI Threats Increase</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI&#8217;s quickly growing uptake has changed everything regarding how security challenges appear. Now, for example, a bad actor with the correct automated approach can quickly identify weaknesses and trigger complex attacks quicker than a manual method, increasing automation around security assessment.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Horizon3 reported approximately 120% annual recurring revenue growth and said it approached $100 million in annual recurring revenue last year. The company serves between 7,200 and 7,300 customers globally, ranging from managed service providers to some of the world&#8217;s largest enterprises.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest funding will also support the development of AI learning loops that allow defensive AI systems to continuously improve by analysing emerging attack techniques. This should support enterprises’ efforts in shifting from just vulnerability awareness to the capability to automatically remedy its most significant security threats. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As new cyber threats emerge at a “machine-speed” pace and sophistication, the company sees AI-powered security testing become indispensable for enterprises determined to guard essential assets and proprietary data, the company asserts.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
