					<description><![CDATA[<p>Dash Bio Raises $30 Million To Expand Automated Bioanalysis Platform Life sciences venture firms invested to accelerate innovation across Dash Bio&#8217;s Automated Bioanalysis Platform for pharmaceutical companies. Oak HC/FT led</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/dash-bio-raises-30-million/" data-wpel-link="internal">Dash Bio Raises $30 Million to Modernise Drug Development Infrastructure</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Dash Bio Raises $30 Million To Expand Automated Bioanalysis Platform</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Life sciences venture firms invested to accelerate innovation across Dash Bio&#8217;s Automated Bioanalysis Platform for pharmaceutical companies. Oak HC/FT led the $30 million round alongside existing investors Freestyle Capital and Swift Ventures successfully together.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Dash Bio will expand laboratory capabilities, enhance proprietary software, and introduce additional bioanalysis testing services globally. The platform accelerates drug discovery by increasing testing capacity across early and late-stage therapeutic development programmes.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Laboratory Expansion And Platform Growth</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Dash Bio said its headquarters will support commercial growth, laboratory expansion, and broader bioanalysis service offerings globally. The company continues developing its proprietary laboratory operating system using robotics and advanced automation technologies continuously worldwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Bioanalysis remains among healthcare&#8217;s longest, most complex, and expensive processes determining treatment safety and effectiveness during development. Despite automation elsewhere, </span><a href="https://www.tandfonline.com/journals/ibio20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">bioanalysis</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> still depends heavily on manual operations and paper-based laboratory data management systems.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its automated system reduces laboratory testing timelines from months to days through modernised scientific workflow automation technology. Dash Bio built an automation-first platform reducing laboratory turnaround times while improving pricing transparency and customer traceability significantly.</span></p>
<h2><b>Technology Accelerates Drug Development Workflows<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203949" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203949" class="size-full wp-image-203949" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/create-a-futuristic-neon-lit-poster-with_N4B60VM8VlOdWss5FtQ-3Q_L7hc_-OcR92hlvquGAH5yw_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing robotic laboratory systems performing automated bioanalysis." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203949" class="wp-caption-text">Dash Bio enables faster drug development through automated, high-efficiency laboratory testing. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Dash Bio operates a 24,000-square-foot GLP facility using robotic workcells controlled by proprietary software automation. The platform supports ELISA, MSD, qPCR, ddPCR, and LC-MS assays while reducing laboratory time and manual effort.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Unlike conventional CROs, Dash Bio delivers preclinical testing results within days instead of several months consistently. The platform helps pharmaceutical developers accelerate timelines while improving project budgets and overall research efficiency significantly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief executive Dave Johnson, chief operating officer Ander Tallett, and chief scientific officer Ely Porter founded Dash Bio. They established the company believing scientific progress should determine development timelines instead of laboratory process limitations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/zenity-raises-125-million/" data-wpel-link="internal">Zenity Raises $125 Million to Expand AI Agent Security Platform</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Customer Growth Reflects Demand For Faster Bioanalysis</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Dash Bio has gained significant commercial traction since launching its go-to-market strategy around nine months ago. The company has secured contracts with more than 30 customers, including four of the world&#8217;s top 15 pharmaceutical companies.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Customers have highlighted the platform&#8217;s rapid turnaround times and transparent pricing as key advantages over traditional laboratory service providers. These capabilities are becoming increasingly valuable as pharmaceutical companies seek faster clinical development and more efficient research operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Oak HC/FT cited the founding team&#8217;s experience building digital and automation infrastructure at Moderna as an important factor behind its investment. The firm&#8217;s partners believe Dash Bio has developed a scalable platform capable of transforming laboratory services for modern drug development.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As pharmaceutical companies continue adopting advanced technologies throughout research and development, demand for automated laboratory infrastructure is expected to increase. Dash Bio plans to use the new funding to strengthen its position in this growing market while helping customers bring new medicines to patients more quickly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights</span></p>
