					<description><![CDATA[<p>Base Power has announced the launch of one of the largest and most powerful home batteries, Base Core. The launch comes as Base Power raises $1 billion to put batteries</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/base-power-1b-series-d-base-core-battery/" data-wpel-link="internal">Base Power Raises $1 Billion To Mass Produce Batteries For Homes in the U.S</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span>Base Power has </span><a href="https://x.com/JLopas/status/2084260590239818184" data-wpel-link="external" rel="external noopener noreferrer"><span>announced</span></a><span> the launch of one of the largest and most powerful home batteries, Base Core. The launch comes as Base Power raises $1 billion to put batteries in people’s homes in the United States. The timing is perfect. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The U.S power system is currently bearing a lot more than it has been in a while. AI data centers are pulling giveaways. EVs are plugging in everywhere. Opting to build new gas plants will take years, and utilities don’t exactly have all the time in the world. Base’s recommendation is to fix this from people’s homes. </span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">The Base Power Product: Base Core</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203939" style="width: 990px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203939" class="size-full wp-image-203939" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Base-core-battery.jpeg" alt="A sleek, light-gray rectangular Base Core battery unit with rounded top edges sitting on a concrete warehouse floor inside a manufacturing facility." width="980" height="981" /><p id="caption-attachment-203939" class="wp-caption-text">Base Core Battery</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">At 39.2kWh, Base Core is one of the largest single home batteries in the market. You can link two for 78.4 kWh and trust it to run your house for several days. In addition to the size, Base Core is not a backup box. It is designed to be part of the grid from the first day. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Base Core is a home battery designed to do two things simultaneously. The first is to keep your lights on when there’s an outage, and to help your power grid remain stable when demand spikes.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This boils down to three things: It installs in less than one hour, so deployment can scale without too many electricians; it switches over automatically when power goes out, and it can stand extreme weather; finally, it is affordable.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Core is made in America, Base Factory 1 in Austin, to be precise. According to the company, the population can expect thousands of units each month. Because it is made in America, buyers don’t have to deal with supply chains or wait months before getting their batteries. </span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/olix-raises-312m-3-3b-valuation-nvidia-rival/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Olix Raises $312M To Scale Specialized AI Inference Silicon</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">The Business Model</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Base has been working on Core for about a year. It is now over 500 kWh deployed and has expanded outside of Texas into Illinois. It is also in partnership with deals such as El Paso Electric and CoServ for more than 200 MW of capacity. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">So, income comes in from two sources: selling and installing the battery and getting paid by utilities to run it. If you own a home, the appeal is outage protection plus less bills. For utilities, the appeal is megawatts now, not later.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/revoy-raises-27-million-electric-truck-dolly/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Revoy Raises $27M to Turn Old Diesel Trucks Into Hybrids</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">What Base Power Aims To Achieve</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">A $1 billion round is not regular for energy hardware, and the same goes for the valuation. It’s less normal. The round was led by Ribbit, Addition, Valor Equity Partners, and JPMorganChase’s Strategic Investment Group. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Altimeter, Coatue, a16z, Thrive, Lightspeed, and more are also in. The JPMorgan angle is telling. They’re putting this money in through their Security and Resiliency Initiative. Their framing isn’t centered around consumer tech, but infrastructure. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Distributed batteries are in their category of transmission lines and substations. Base has raised more than $2.5 billion in total. The funds will be allocated to building more Cores, hiring more experts, and expanding into more cities.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/simile-raises-200-million-agentic-twin-consumer-simulations/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Simile Raises $200M for Building Agentic Twin Simulations</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/base-power-1b-series-d-base-core-battery/" data-wpel-link="internal">Base Power Raises $1 Billion To Mass Produce Batteries For Homes in the U.S</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
