		<title>Olix Raises $312M at $3.3B Valuation To Scale Specialized AI Inference Silicon</title>
		<link>https://ventureburn.com/olix-raises-312m-3-3b-valuation-nvidia-rival/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Ekemini]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 14:23:14 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Startup]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI agents]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI Chip]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[artificial intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Olix]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Series B]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://ventureburn.com/?p=203932</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>As AI has exploded over the last few years, there have been different types of AI chips designed to solve different tasks. Olix raises $312 million to create one chip</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/olix-raises-312m-3-3b-valuation-nvidia-rival/" data-wpel-link="internal">Olix Raises $312M at $3.3B Valuation To Scale Specialized AI Inference Silicon</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As AI has exploded over the last few years, there have been different types of AI chips designed to solve different tasks. Olix </span><a href="https://x.com/jamesdacombe/status/2084226267008663823" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">raises</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> $312 million to create one chip that handles every part of an AI model’s work. New York firm Fundomo led the round, with Arm, Hudson River Trading, and Netflix co-founder Reed Hastings joining as angel investors. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Existing backers Hummingbird Ventures, Crane, Plural, Creandum, Phoenix Court, and Transition all put in more money too. The result is a $3.3 billion increase, which has tripled the roughly $1 billion mark Olix hit just six months ago when it raised $220 million.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Why Olix Was Founded</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203934" style="width: 776px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203934" class="size-full wp-image-203934" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/James-Dacombe.jpeg" alt="A headshot, right-placed headshot of the Olix founder, James Dacombe" width="766" height="400" /><p id="caption-attachment-203934" class="wp-caption-text">James Dacombe. Credit: Olix</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">James Dacombe started Olix in London in 2024, in his early twenties, after building an earlier company focused on brain monitoring technology. His argument to investors is that Nvidia’s general-purpose chips are hitting a wall.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Dacombe believes a data center running AI inference is really a factory that produces tokens, he says, and every token needs hundreds of different operations. Unfortunately, most companies still run all of them through the same chip.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/revoy-raises-27-million-electric-truck-dolly/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Revoy Raises $27M to Turn Old Diesel Trucks Into Hybrids</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Splitting the Work Across Specialists</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Olix’s answer is X-1. It spreads a model’s workload across several chips instead of muzzling one processor. The chips talk to each other using light instead of copper wiring, which Olix says cuts latency and power draw. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its first chip, DX-1, handles the decode stage. This is the point where a model actually generates its output. In a modelPlus of a 100 billion parameter, the company claims it can generate over 10,000 tokens per second per user using less power than a regular chip would at the same batch size. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Olix says the same architecture is built to scale to models with 10 trillion parameters or more. One detail matters beyond the performance claims: Olix’s design skips advanced packaging and high-bandwidth memory.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These are two of the most supply-constrained components in the chip industry right now. That’s a deliberate choice to avoid getting stuck in the same supply queues as everyone else chasing Nvidia.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/simile-raises-200-million-agentic-twin-consumer-simulations/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Simile Raises $200M for Building Agentic Twin Simulations</i></b></a></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400">Hiring to Match the Ambition</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Pumped from the raise, Olix has hired two experts. Matt Briers and Nick McKeown now join the board. Briers is former Wise CFO, and McKeown is popular for co-inventing software-defined networking and OpenFlow. This presupposes that the founder is very particular about scaling.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">A Crowded Race to Replace Nvidia</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Olix isn’t the only startup chasing this opportunity. Bristol-based Fractile was able to raise $220 million in May with support from Accel and Founders Fund. Next to those numbers, Olix’s $3.3 billion, even after tripling in six months, still looks like the smaller player in the room.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI chips are already an $84B industry. By 2030, the market will more than triple. There’s a massive demand and cause to pay attention to Olix. Olix now has over 140 employees across London, Bristol, Toronto, Austin, and San Francisco. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company plans to make DX-1 accessible to customers in the second half of 2027. Whether the throughput numbers hold up outside a pitch deck will matter far more than the size of this round.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/k2-space-raises-500m-6-8-billion-valuation/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>K2 Space Raises $500M To Scale Large, High-Power Satellites</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/olix-raises-312m-3-3b-valuation-nvidia-rival/" data-wpel-link="internal">Olix Raises $312M at $3.3B Valuation To Scale Specialized AI Inference Silicon</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
