					<description><![CDATA[<p>Series C Funding Accelerates Manufacturing Expansion Antora Energy raised $550 million in Series C funding to accelerate thermal battery adoption across the United States. The company will increase manufacturing and</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/antora-energy-raises-550m/" data-wpel-link="internal">Antora Energy Raises $550M To Expand Thermal Battery Production For AI And Industry</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Series C Funding Accelerates Manufacturing Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antora Energy raised $550 million in Series C funding to accelerate thermal battery adoption across the United States. The company will increase manufacturing and build a second domestic production facility supporting larger energy storage projects. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These projects will serve industrial sites, data centres, and investor-owned utility companies across the United States. G2 Venture Partners and Eclipse co-led the funding round alongside numerous prominent institutional and strategic investors. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Investors included Ribbit Capital, Salesforce Ventures, Activate Capital, John Doerr, and Westly Group among others. Additional investors included StepStone Group, Liberty Mutual Strategic Ventures, Decarbonization Partners, and Lowercarbon Capital together successfully. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antora Energy will accelerate </span><a href="https://www.wtsenergy.com/glossary/utility-scale/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">utility-scale</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> deployments while expanding manufacturing capacity and commissioning another United States production facility. The company also aims to strengthen domestic supply chains supporting industrial customers and rapidly growing artificial intelligence data centres. </span></p>
<h2><b>Thermal Batteries Target Growing Energy Demand</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antora Energy develops thermal batteries storing inexpensive grid electricity as heat within insulated solid carbon blocks efficiently. The stored thermal energy can later provide industrial heat or generate electricity whenever customers require reliable power. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antora said its systems use common materials instead of difficult-to-source rare earth minerals for manufacturing efficiency. The company added its modular factory-built design enables faster production and shorter installation times than conventional infrastructure. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its thermal batteries serve industrial customers including chemical manufacturers, food producers, steel plants, utilities, and artificial intelligence data centres. Antora said customers reduce electricity costs by storing inexpensive power and selling electricity during peak demand. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company recently deployed what it describes as one of the world&#8217;s largest battery storage projects, a 5-gigawatt-hour system in South Dakota that progressed from construction to energy delivery in less than twelve months.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI Data Centres Drive Clean Energy Investment<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203898" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203898" class="size-full wp-image-203898" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/a-futuristic-vibrant-poster-showcases-a-_-PuO6L4dVwaE_JB40iJ2ng_tKHrrU2oTp2QUx7A1uFk_g_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing thermal battery systems powering AI data centres and large-scale manufacturing facilities." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203898" class="wp-caption-text">Rising AI energy demand drives expansion of thermal battery production and clean power infrastructure. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Artificial intelligence&#8217;s rapid growth and electricity demand are placing increasing pressure on existing United States power systems. Data centres are driving significant growth in electricity demand across the United States, according to The Times. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Companies increasingly seek reliable, deployable, non-emitting power sources reducing dependence on fossil fuels for future operations. The Times reported Antora believes its thermal batteries offer faster, lower-cost energy storage than conventional batteries. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company&#8217;s manufacturing campus in San Jose has recently expanded into a three-building facility that ranks among the largest battery gigafactories in the United States. The new funding will allow Antora to replicate that manufacturing capability through a second domestic production facility while supporting additional engineering, manufacturing, and construction jobs.<br />
</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/xsight-labs-raises-over-300m/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Xsight Labs Raises Over $300M At $2.8 Billion Valuation To Expand AI Networking Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Investors Back Next Generation Energy Storage</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The oversubscribed financing demonstrates continued investor confidence in energy storage technologies despite slower venture investment across the broader clean technology sector. Demand for flexible storage solutions has continued to increase as renewable electricity generation expands and industrial energy consumption grows.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antora&#8217;s ability to serve both heavy industry and AI infrastructure positions the company within two of the fastest-growing energy markets. Its modular systems can provide continuous heat or electricity without depending on fuel deliveries or complex construction projects.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As industries seek practical ways to decarbonise operations while meeting rising electricity demand, Antora plans to accelerate commercial deployments and expand manufacturing capacity across the United States. </span></p>
